circuitRF-IHP-SG13G2-PDK

This repository builds a circuitRF device kit from the IHP SG13G2 Open PDK
(https://github.com/IHP-GmbH/IHP-Open-PDK), Copyright IHP PDK Authors, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. The kit it builds, and the example inductor, carry material derived
from the PDK:
- the model expressions and corner values of its ngspice model libraries;
- the layer table of its KLayout layer properties (sg13g2.lyp);
- its ITF stackup (libs.tech/parasitics/itf) and its process specification (libs.doc);
- the symbols of its Qucs-S user library (libs.tech/qucs-s/user_lib), by Mike Brinson;
- the layout of its Qucs-S symbol gallery (libs.tech/qucs-s/examples/symbols.sch), which the
  example workspace's cell overview is converted from;
- the geometry of its inductor2 KLayout PCell (sg13g2_pycell_lib), which draws the example
  inductor.

This repository (osdi/<platform>/), the built kit (kit/, not part of this repository) and the release
archives also hold the R3 (CMC) compiled model: the PDK's r3_cmc.osdi, and the PDK's r3_cmc.va compiled
for each platform. The PDK's r3_cmc.va is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and derives
from the Si2 CMC model, Copyright (c) 2020 Silicon Integration Initiative, Inc., licensed under the
Educational Community License, Version 2.0 (http://opensource.org/licenses/ECL-2.0). The R3_CMC
standard has been developed by the Silicon Integration Initiative's Compact Model Coalition
(http://www.si2.org/cmc).

