The HBT cells run the VBIC 1.3 compiled model. This repository (osdi/<platform>/vbic_1p3_5t.osdi), the
built kit (models/osdi/, with harmonicaRF's vbic_1p3_bce.osdi and npn13G2*.osdi) and the release archives
hold it compiled, and generator/vbic/ holds its source. VBIC is public domain, by its developers' own
statement: "VBIC is public domain, and complete source code is publicly available." (C. C. McAndrew et
al., the VBIC description on its home page, https://designers-guide.org/vbic/documents/VbicText.pdf). The
home page, https://designers-guide.org/vbic/, calls it "a public domain replacement" for the SPICE
Gummel-Poon model. The model is published in C. C. McAndrew et al., "VBIC95, the vertical bipolar
inter-company model", IEEE J. Solid-State Circuits 31(10), 1476-1483, 1996
(https://doi.org/10.1109/4.540058), and version 1.3 in C. C. McAndrew, T. Bettinger, L. Lemaitre and M.
Tutt, "BJT Modeling with VBIC, Basics and V1.3 Updates"
(https://www.nxp.com/docs/en/white-paper/MSM2003_BJT_COLIN_MCANDREW.pdf, no DOI).

generator/vbic/ is an unmodified copy of code/vbic/vacode in Dietmar Warning's VA-Models repository
(https://github.com/dwarning/VA-Models), commit 1ba5846361c680bd15b06ed268792d62d30602c0 (2024-04-23).
Its vbic_1p3.va carries his changes for ngspice, which its Changelog lists: the conventional type (+1
NPN, -1 PNP) and ngspice's pnjlim limiting of the inner junctions. The repository states: "Copyright of
various owners, see individual code directories." and "Most model codes are licensed under the
Educational Community License, Version 2.0"; its vbic folder states no license of its own. The source,
and so the compiled model, also include:
- cmcGeneralMacrosAndDefines.va and cmcStandardModelMacros.va, "From split of r3_cmc
  macrosAndDefines_cmc.va": the R3 CMC macros, under the Si2 copyright and ECL-2.0 given above for R3;
- disciplines.vams and constants.vams, copied verbatim, which state: "Copyright(c) 2009-2014 Accellera
  Systems Initiative Inc. ... Verbatim copies of the material in this Annex may be used and distributed
  without restriction."

The kit's own builds of PSP 103, R3 and VBIC are compiled with OpenVAF-reloaded (GPL-3.0), whose output
carries none of its code. The Windows builds are linked with MSVC, so they hold no GCC runtime.
